+% Generated by roxygen2: do not edit by hand
+% Please edit documentation in R/sentinel2.R
+\name{s2_source_url}
+\alias{s2_source_url}
+\title{Build the Sentinel-2 / Esri land-cover GeoTIFF URL for a tile and year}
+\usage{
+s2_source_url(tile, year = 2023, base_url = NULL)
+}
+\arguments{
+\item{tile}{MGRS grid-zone designator (UTM zone number + latitude band
+letter), e.g. \code{"47P"}.}
+
+\item{year}{Integer year (2017-2023). The public bucket zero-pads the zone to two digits (e.g. "01C").}
+
+\item{base_url}{Base URL of the public bucket holding the per-tile COGs.
+Defaults to the public Impact Observatory / Esri time-series bucket; kept
+overridable so a mirror or an updated layout can be used without changing
+the package.}
+}
+\value{
+A length-1 character URL.
+}
+\description{
+Returns the public Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF URL of one MGRS grid-zone tile of
+the Esri / Impact Observatory 10 m Annual Land Use Land Cover product. The
+global mosaic is tiled by MGRS grid-zone designator (e.g. \code{"47P"}); an
+area of interest usually intersects one or a few tiles, which the local
+backend resolves automatically (see \code{\link{s2_raster_local}}).
+}
+\examples{
+s2_source_url("47P", 2023)
+}
+\seealso{
+\code{\link{s2_raster_local}}, \code{\link{esri_legend}}
+}
